A||N||8||KissMySSFiero||Driving a salvage title car from Illinois?  ||||1||
Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||10-10-2001||07:33 AM||||does anyone here know if you can tag a car with a salvage title.  i think the car im looking at has an Illinios title.  I would want an Indiana tag.  if it makes a difference the car was titled for mechanical reasons not a wreck.  TIA<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-10-2001||02:08 PM||||I suggest that you check directly with your state DMV.  Here in Minn. you can tag & drive a vehicle with a salvage tag- you just usually can't get bank financing to buy it.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-10-2001||02:23 PM||||The car needs to be inspected by a State cop.<BR>He will sign it off as repaired. When you get a new title it will say 'rebuilt'.<BR>What was the damage? Determines what paperwork you need.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-10-2001||06:41 PM||||There's a form you can get at the license branch.  You fill it out as you fix things.  When you're done, turn it back into the license branch.  They might require a cop to inspect the car (but probably not for mechanical damage--what can they see?) then you can apply for a regular title.||||reg||1
Z||000004||KissMySSFiero||10-10-2001||06:44 PM||||The car is in a junkyard and its complete.  never wrecked by what i can see.  the paint is still shining.  and interior is perfect minus the drivers seat, but its only got a dime size whole.  its an 86Se with auto and V6.  every power option.  if i can get it for a couple hundred it would make a nice daily driver car.   the guy at the junkyard said i can get a salvage title but says it cant be driven again.  I guess ill call the dmv tomorrow.  Thanks for the help.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||10-10-2001||07:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>The car is in a junkyard and its complete.  never wrecked by what i can see.  the paint is still shining.  and interior is perfect minus the drivers seat, but its only got a dime size whole.  its an 86Se with auto and V6.  every power option.  if i can get it for a couple hundred it would make a nice daily driver car.   the guy at the junkyard said i can get a salvage title but says it cant be driven again.  I guess ill call the dmv tomorrow.  Thanks for the help.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Kiss!<BR>I have a salvage title on my Fiero...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||10-11-2001||08:12 PM||||This varies greatly by state. Some states require special inspections before such cars are allowed to have a new tag. You really want to check this carefully with both DMV's involved. The reason is you'll likely need some sort of temp tag to drive it home.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||10-11-2001||09:29 PM||||Sounds to me like that Fiero went swimming... BE VERY CAREFUL about that. No physical damage usually means something more sinister. If the water's hit any of the electrical ( and it probably has) expect nightmare electrical gremlins. Check the underside for mud buildup, and any corners. Check to find water-lines in the car, inspect the interior CLOSELY. Look for any signs of water damage. The only other thing it could be is a curb-wipeout that wrecked a wheel and tweeked the frame? Do your homework!!!||||reg||10
Z||000008||LarryB||10-11-2001||09:42 PM||||Several other people have already given you good information. The info you got from the salvage guy isn't correct.<P>Depending on the state you live in, a salvage title simply means the car was either totaled at some point or it had been sold previously as a parts car.  <P>Once you have a salvage title you cannot legally get a new regular title issued against the vehicle, at least nowhere I know of, only new salvage titles. That doesn't mean the car can't be repaired and made safe to drive again although it will affect any resale value.<P>You may also need to place a permanent sticker or tag in a conspicuous place identifying the vehicle as being a former salvage or insurance total.<BR>||||reg||1
